[statement]
A package whose condition holds, and whose dependency only packages ruled
out could meet, is passed over: `f`, installed first, holds `K`, so `s1`,
the one provider of `S`, is ruled out, and so is `e`, which needs `S`.
Contrast `an-unmet-dependency-refuses-the-request`, where nothing ever
provides the name.

[repository]
P:base
V:1

P:f
V:1
p:K=1

P:s1
V:1
p:S=1 K=1

P:e
V:1
i:base
D:S

[request]
base
f

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install base 1
install f 1
